WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.625
Before the twentieth century, people were able to view moving pictures.

2
00:00:04.575 --> 00:00:07.725
Those moving pictures were then named films.

3
00:00:07.725 --> 00:00:11.700
At about the same time, films were actually very short.

4
00:00:11.700 --> 00:00:23.250
Subjects usually included views of a couple of people having breakfast, a kid playing with a banana, a man doing exercises, a pig eating an egg, or even just several houses, all very simple ideas.

5
00:00:23.250 --> 00:00:27.925
In other words, the early films were extremely physical and casual.

6
00:00:27.925 --> 00:00:33.425
Then people started expressing their feelings, nervous or anxious, and their thoughts in films.

7
00:00:33.425 --> 00:00:39.312
Later, conversations and interviews showed up in films, people call those films documentary.

8
00:00:39.312 --> 00:00:45.087
With the diversity of contents, it appeared genres, but few films lasted more than an hour.

9
00:00:45.087 --> 00:00:49.375
By 1914, national film industries were established.

10
00:00:49.375 --> 00:00:55.562
The great strength of Italian industry was historical epic, with large casts and massive scenery.

11
00:00:55.562 --> 00:01:03.237
The First World War definitely retarded the film industry in Europe, Meanwhile, the American industry grew in relative importance.

12
00:01:03.237 --> 00:01:08.075
Filmmakers in the US earned millions of dollars, become rich and famous.

13
00:01:08.075 --> 00:01:12.162
But the facts behind were revealed to be extremely commercial.

14
00:01:12.162 --> 00:01:16.812
During the 1960s, the cinema of France became powerful.

15
00:01:16.812 --> 00:01:21.825
French New Wave directors broke the rules of Hollywood cinema narrative structure.

16
00:01:21.825 --> 00:01:25.812
Such as campus life, urbanity, or horror stories.

17
00:01:25.812 --> 00:01:33.525
With the worldwide film boom, cinema probably became the most important tool of communication, and entertainment, and mass media.

18
00:01:33.525 --> 00:01:41.637
Cinema companies knew how to market a movie, for some special occasions like Christmas, they would generally make blockbusters on shown in theaters.

19
00:01:41.637 --> 00:01:46.800
Additionally, filmmakers would offer trailers for audiences to have a quick preview.

20
00:01:46.800 --> 00:01:58.337
Moreover, you could see more and more inserted advertisement in films, such as Nestle milk and Diet Coke.It was regarded as an interesting phenomenon that recently filmmakers from Korea got remarkable in Asia.
